<title>FRANCE: ADP-Paris airport export traffic up 0.7pct in Jan.</title>
<headline>ADP-Paris airport export traffic up 0.7pct in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air cargo exports from the two Paris airports, Charle de Gaulle and Orly,totalled 41,577 tonnes in January 1997, up 0.7 percent on the same month last year, airport authority figures (ADP) show.</p>
<p>January 1997 ADP export traffic, by region, with percentage change on January 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p>			     JAN '97     PCT CHANGE</p>
<p> Domestic		   3,667     down   3.0pct</p>
<p> European Union	   5,229     up    14.6</p>
<p> Non-EU Europe		894     up     2.5</p>
<p> North Africa		 809     down   8.2</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa     3,530     up     5.3</p>
<p> North America	   10,400     down   2.2</p>
<p> French territories     2,020     down   3.9</p>
<p> Latin America	    2,276     up    11.0</p>
<p> Middle East		4,283     up    10.9</p>
<p> Far East		   8,469     down   8.1</p>
<p> Total		     41,577     up     0.7</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax</p>
